.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
.Dd October 12, 2026
.Dt DTFL_DOGS_PROPOSE 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm dtfl_dogs_propose ,
.Nm dtfl_dogs_propose_distinct ,
.Nm dtfl_dogs_validate ,
.Nm dtfl_dogs_count
.Nd prefix-extension operators for delta queries
.Sh LIBRARY
Timely and differential dataflow library
.Pq libdtfl , \-ldtfl
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In dtfl/dogs.h
.Ft dtfl_collection *
.Fn dtfl_dogs_propose "dtfl_collection *prefixes" "dtfl_arranged *arr" "const dtfl_type *out_type" "dtfl_key_selector_fn key" "dtfl_ctx ctx"
.Ft dtfl_collection *
.Fn dtfl_dogs_propose_distinct "dtfl_collection *prefixes" "dtfl_arranged *arr" "const dtfl_type *out_type" "dtfl_key_selector_fn key" "dtfl_ctx ctx"
.Ft dtfl_collection *
.Fn dtfl_dogs_validate "dtfl_collection *extensions" "dtfl_arranged *arr" "const dtfl_type *out_type" "const dtfl_type *prefix_type" "const dtfl_type *val_type" "dtfl_key_selector_fn key" "dtfl_ctx ctx"
.Ft dtfl_collection *
.Fn dtfl_dogs_count "dtfl_collection *prefixes" "dtfl_arranged *arr" "const dtfl_type *prefix_type" "dtfl_key_selector_fn key" "dtfl_ctx ctx" "uint64_t index"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
These are the operators the generic join
.Pq Xr dtfl_collection_extend 3
is built from.
They may also be used directly to wire a delta query by hand.
Each selects a key from a prefix with
.Va key
and reads the arrangement
.Va arr
at trace times less or equal to the prefix's own time, the lattice order
that, under an AltNeu scope, makes each pair of concurrent updates interact
exactly once.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_dogs_propose
extends each prefix with every value the arrangement holds under the
prefix's key, scaling the prefix diff by the matched count.
.Fn dtfl_dogs_propose_distinct
does the same but leaves the diff unscaled.
.Va arr
is a key \[->] value arrangement, and the output records are
.Va prefix Ns Li || Ns value
of
.Va out_type .
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_dogs_validate
keeps each
.Va prefix Ns Li || Ns value
extension whose
.Pq Fn key "prefix" , value
pair is present in
.Va arr ,
a
.Pq key , value
\[->] unit arrangement arranged by self.
.Va prefix_type
splits the extension into its prefix and value parts.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_dogs_count
annotates each prefix triple
.Pq prefix , count , index ,
where the count and index are two u64 words following the prefix, with the
fewer of its current count and the number of extensions
.Va arr
offers under the prefix's key; when the arrangement offers fewer, the
triple's index is overwritten with
.Va index .
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Each function returns a new
.Vt dtfl_collection
the caller frees with
.Fn dtfl_collection_free ,
or
.Dv NULL
with
.Dv DTFL_EALGEBRA
when the diff classes do not multiply.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr dtfl_collection_extend 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_collection_index_new 3
.Sh STANDARDS
A C11 port of the dogsdogsdogs
.Pa src/operators/propose.rs ,
.Pa src/operators/validate.rs
and
.Pa src/operators/count.rs .
